#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:6
msgid "Implementing custom interfaces - how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:8
msgid ""
"When predefined interface definitions are not enough, you need to create "
"custom interfaces. In this article, you will learn how to define and build "
"interfaces with different field types. This will help you implement custom "
"interfaces in ROS to suit your needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:12
msgid ""
"**Area: Framework | Content-type: how-to | Experience: beginner, "
"intermediate**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:16
msgid "Contents"
msgstr "目次"

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:19
msgid "Summary"
msgstr "摘要"

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:21
msgid ""
"Interfaces define how nodes exchange data. ROS offers three main interface "
"types:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:24
msgid "Topics (``.msg`` files)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:25
msgid "Services (``.srv`` files)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:26
msgid "Actions (``.action`` files)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:28
msgid ""
"`Learn more about interfaces <https://docs.ros.org/en/rolling/Concepts/Basic/"
"Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.html>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:30
msgid "Before creating a custom interface, do the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:32
msgid "Check whether a suitable standard message already exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:33
msgid ""
"If no single standard message fits your use case, consider creating a new "
"message composed of standard messages. See standard messages here: https://"
"github.com/ros2/common_interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:36
msgid "Creating a completely custom message should be the last resort."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:38
msgid ""
"Creating custom interfaces involves preparing a package, specifying "
"interface definitions, and registering the interfaces in ``package.xml`` and "
"``CMakeLists.txt``. Using custom interfaces involves configuring a node to "
"include the interfaces in its source, and configuring the node to build with "
"the interfaces in ``CMakeLists.txt``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:43
msgid ""
"The best practice is to declare interfaces in dedicated interface packages, "
"but sometimes it may be more convenient for you to declare, create and use "
"an interface all in one package. Using a dedicated interface package is "
"preferred because it allows multiple packages to share message definitions "
"without sharing any other code contained in the package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:47
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr "先備條件"

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:49
msgid ""
":doc:`Install ROS </Get-Started/Installation>`, and create your :doc:"
"`workspace </ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/"
"Creating-A-Workspace/Creating-A-Workspace>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:50
msgid ""
"Make sure you understand how to :doc:`create packages </ROS-Framework/client-"
"libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Creating-Your-First-ROS2-Package>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:53
msgid "Steps"
msgstr "步驟"

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:57
msgid ""
"For our examples, we are using the ``msg`` interface type, but the steps "
"below apply to all interface types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:59
msgid ""
"In your workspace ``src`` folder, create a ``more_interfaces`` CMake package "
"with a folder for interface definitions. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:62
msgid ""
"$ ros2 pkg create --build-type ament_cmake more_interfaces\n"
"$ mkdir -p more_interfaces/msg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:69
msgid ""
"In ROS 2, interfaces can only be defined in CMake packages. You can also use "
"`ament_cmake_python <https://github.com/ament/ament_cmake/tree/rolling/"
"ament_cmake_python>`__ to include Python libraries and nodes in a CMake "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:72
msgid ""
"In your interface definitions folder, create a file in which you provide the "
"definitions for the interface. For example, for a message interface, you can "
"create an ``AddressBook.msg`` file that collects personal data: The "
"``PHONE_TYPE_*`` constants in this example form an enumerated type pattern "
"for ``phone_type`` values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:76
msgid ""
"uint8 PHONE_TYPE_HOME=0\n"
"uint8 PHONE_TYPE_WORK=1\n"
"uint8 PHONE_TYPE_MOBILE=2\n"
"string first_name\n"
"string last_name\n"
"string phone_number\n"
"uint8 phone_type\n"
"geometry_msgs/Point location"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:87
msgid ""
"In ``package.xml``, add the following code to register your package as part "
"of interface groups: ``rosidl_default_generators``: Needed to generate the "
"code during the build. ``rosidl_default_runtime``: Needed only at run time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:91
msgid ""
"<build_depend>rosidl_default_generators</build_depend>\n"
"<exec_depend>rosidl_default_runtime</exec_depend>\n"
"<depend>geometry_msgs</depend>\n"
"<member_of_group>rosidl_interface_packages</member_of_group>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:98
msgid ""
"In ``CMakeLists.txt``, add the required code to make the runtime libraries "
"available and to generate source files from your interface definition. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:101
msgid ""
"find_package(rosidl_default_generators REQUIRED)\n"
"find_package(geometry_msgs REQUIRED)\n"
"set(msg_files \"msg/AddressBook.msg\")\n"
"rosidl_generate_interfaces(${PROJECT_NAME} ${msg_files}\n"
"  DEPENDENCIES geometry_msgs\n"
")\n"
"ament_export_dependencies(rosidl_default_runtime)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:111
msgid ""
"In the ``more_interfaces/src`` folder, create a node to interact with your "
"new interface. For example, for a message interface, create "
"``publish_address_book.cpp`` with code to publish the message periodically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:114
msgid ""
"#include <chrono>\n"
"#include <memory>\n"
"\n"
"#include \"rclcpp/rclcpp.hpp\"\n"
"#include \"more_interfaces/msg/address_book.hpp\"\n"
"\n"
"using namespace std::chrono_literals;\n"
"\n"
"class AddressBookPublisher : public rclcpp::Node\n"
"{\n"
"public:\n"
"  AddressBookPublisher()\n"
"  : Node(\"address_book_publisher\")\n"
"  {\n"
"    address_book_publisher_ =\n"
"      this->create_publisher<more_interfaces::msg::"
"AddressBook>(\"address_book\", 10);\n"
"\n"
"    auto publish_msg = [this]() -> void {\n"
"        auto message = more_interfaces::msg::AddressBook();\n"
"\n"
"        message.first_name = \"John\";\n"
"        message.last_name = \"Doe\";\n"
"        message.phone_number = \"1234567890\";\n"
"        message.phone_type = message.PHONE_TYPE_MOBILE;\n"
"        message.location.x = 37.7749;\n"
"        message.location.y = -122.4194;\n"
"        message.location.z = 0.0;\n"
"\n"
"        std::cout << \"Publishing Contact\\nFirst:\" << message.first_name "
"<<\n"
"          \"  Last:\" << message.last_name << std::endl;\n"
"\n"
"        this->address_book_publisher_->publish(message);\n"
"      };\n"
"    timer_ = this->create_wall_timer(1s, publish_msg);\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"
"private:\n"
"  rclcpp::Publisher<more_interfaces::msg::AddressBook>::SharedPtr "
"address_book_publisher_;\n"
"  rclcpp::TimerBase::SharedPtr timer_;\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"int main(int argc, char * argv[])\n"
"{\n"
"  rclcpp::init(argc, argv);\n"
"  rclcpp::spin(std::make_shared<AddressBookPublisher>());\n"
"  rclcpp::shutdown();\n"
"\n"
"  return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:167
msgid ""
"In ``CMakeLists.txt``, create a new target so the node builds correctly. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:170
msgid ""
"find_package(rclcpp REQUIRED)\n"
"add_executable(publish_address_book src/publish_address_book.cpp)\n"
"target_link_libraries(publish_address_book rclcpp::rclcpp)\n"
"install(TARGETS publish_address_book DESTINATION lib/${PROJECT_NAME})"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:177
msgid "In ``CMakeLists.txt``, link the node to your interface. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Single-Package-Define-And-Use-Interface.rst:180
msgid ""
"rosidl_get_typesupport_target(cpp_typesupport_target ${PROJECT_NAME} "
"rosidl_typesupport_cpp)\n"
"target_link_libraries(publish_address_book \"${cpp_typesupport_target}\")"
msgstr ""

